    rdf:value "him, though she likes to have him make love to her. I may be all wrong, but his passion seems to me, while it is very intense, only by  chance  devoted to her and somewhat  voulu  and literary at that. He says she is “perfectly congenial”, but I hardly know how a young woman who writes her autobiography in the Chronicle and spends her time going to dinners and teas and balls in the journalistic London world – a whole combination of things he, not in love, would  loathe ! – can be “congenial”, adorable as she may be. But his letters have been so very much the typical letters of “a man in love”, that I really have no means of judging. However, I think I am safe – though sad – in predicting that if he does not "^^xsd:string ;
